Ladybird binds Reload Without Cache to Option-Command-R and Command-
Shift-R on macOS, and to Ctrl-Shift-R and Ctrl-F5 on other platforms.
And a Shift-click on the Reload button runs it too. But on the Stop
button that takes its place while a page loads, a Shift-click stops the
load, the same as in Chrome.

Option-Command-R is Safari’s binding. Chrome binds Command-Shift-R on
macOS (accelerators_cocoa.mm), and Ctrl-Shift-R, Ctrl-F5, and Shift-F5
elsewhere (accelerator_table.cc), and ReloadButton::ButtonPressed()
turns a Shift-click or Ctrl-click into IDC_RELOAD_BYPASSING_CACHE.
Firefox’s browser-sets.inc.xhtml binds accel-Shift-R everywhere, and
accel-F5 outside macOS (key_reload_skip_cache, key_reload_skip_cache2),
and BrowserCommands.reloadOrDuplicate() skips the cache on a Shift-
click. The WebKitGTK MiniBrowser binds Ctrl-F5 and Ctrl-Shift-R to its
reload-no-cache action. Ladybird leaves out the Shift-F5 only Chrome
binds, and Chrome’s Ctrl-click on the Reload button.
